# [M5.0] D27 axis 5 -- \p refusals (extract Sec 3.1's 30-measured-error-147
# survey + the 4 block spellings). 34 blocks, ONE case each (a refusal has one
# case -- extract's own note) = 34 cases. These are PERMANENT refusals: once
# 'unicode-props' lands, PCRE2 itself still refuses every one of these bodies
# (error 147, "unknown property name") -- so today's `perr` (currently for the
# module-gate reason) IS this block's enduring correct shape; only the
# diagnostic WORDING changes, which D26 rules out of scope. Confirmed live,
# this cell's libpcre2 10.37 2021-05-26, against BOTH options=0 and PCRE2_UTF.

# axis5 block p-refusal-A | pattern: \p{A} | PCRE2 error 147 (confirmed live, both options=0 and PCRE2_UTF) -- a PERMANENT refusal
pattern \p{A}
perr

